From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 08:36:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: keep the MTP handoff
 of this boot chain

Aurora now cold-starts the J604 MTP (7e00a51866): the loader is asked to
program the dart-mtp filter for a halted MTP through
linux-enablement-mac,dapf-halted-handoff, the MTP and its HID function
move to DART stream 0, and streams 1-3 are remapped to 0.

The m1n1 this J604 boots does not read that property; it hands the MTP
over through linux-enablement-mac,dapf-handoff, and the internal keyboard
and trackpad run on stream 1 with the live MTP bypass retained. Keep that
here until the loader carries the halted-consumer writer, so the keyboard
at the disk passphrase prompt does not depend on an untested handoff.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi | 23 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
index 7cc624ea96..9b96fcb9e7 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
@@ -1479,3 +1479,26 @@
 	reg = <0x00 0x00 0x00 0x00>;
 };
 
+
+/*
+ * Keep the MTP as this boot chain runs it: the loader hands the running MTP
+ * over through linux-enablement-mac,dapf-handoff and Linux keeps it on DART
+ * stream 1. The cold start in t8132-j604.dts needs a loader that programs the
+ * dart-mtp filter for a halted MTP (linux-enablement-mac,dapf-halted-handoff),
+ * which this chain's m1n1 does not read.
+ */
+&{/chosen} {
+	/delete-property/ linux-enablement-mac,dapf-halted-handoff;
+};
+
+&mtp_dart {
+	/delete-property/ apple,remap-streams;
+};
+
+&mtp {
+	iommus = <&mtp_dart 1>;
+};
+
+&mtp_hid {
+	iommus = <&mtp_dart 1>;
+};
